<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  TC8 §4.8.6.1 TCP_BASICS_14: TCP MUST NOT move on to CLOSED state
  from TIME-WAIT state before 2*MSL time expires, where TIME-WAIT
  state is reached through CLOSING state. Derived from NEGATIVE
  "RFC 793 §3.2 p23 Terminology" (MUST).

  v3.0 Test Procedure (p301-p320.txt:50):
    1. TESTER: Cause the DUT to move on to CLOSING state
    2. TESTER: Send ACK for the FIN just received from the DUT
       (DUT moves to TIME-WAIT state)
    3. TESTER: Send a FIN within 2*MSL time
    4. DUT:    Send ACK
  Pass criterion: step 4 (DUT ACKs the within-2*MSL FIN replay,
  proving TIME-WAIT survived).

  Prelude mechanism (CLOSING-path drive to TIME-WAIT): the DUT
  application issues CLOSE, driving the DUT into FIN-WAIT-1 with the
  tester's pure-ACK auto-reply withheld; the tester then injects a
  FIN+ACK whose ack number intentionally does NOT cover the DUT FIN
  — the DUT in FIN-WAIT-1 receives a non-acking FIN and per RFC 793
  §3.9 enters CLOSING (the DUT also emits a pure ACK acknowledging
  the tester FIN). The tester then injects a second segment, an ACK
  that DOES ack the DUT FIN, advancing the DUT silently CLOSING →
  TIME-WAIT. The tester releases its side of the 4-tuple without
  emitting a second tester FIN.

  See tests/_templates/tcp_time_wait_4state.sce-template.xml for
  the shared 4-state observation chain. Per-case thin-shell binds
  mid_label=closing_ack (CLOSING-path semantics — the DUT's ACK
  this state observes responds to tester FIN driving the FW1 →
  CLOSING transition, not the FW2 → TIME-WAIT transition the FW2
  variants observe) and replay_label=replay_ack (within-2*MSL ACK
  observation, 5s deadline).

  Negative smoke flips ipv4.dut_iface_ip → first state's
  src_ip-conjunct unreachable → fail_no_handshake_ack.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       xmlns:cpp="urn:sce:cpp"
       version="1.0"
       name="tcp_basics_14"
       datamodel="null"
       initial="listening_handshake_ack">
  <sce:use template="../_templates/tcp_time_wait_4state.sce-template.xml"
           mid_label="closing_ack"
           mid_fail_reason="no_dut_ack_in_closing_transition"
           replay_label="replay_ack"
           replay_method="is_pure_dut_ack"
           replay_deadline="5s"
           replay_fail_reason="no_dut_ack_to_replay_fin_in_time_wait_via_closing"
           local_offset="kTcpBasics14LocalOffset"/>
</scxml>
